#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:4
msgid "Connect to a session over SSH"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:5
msgid ""
"*Use a terminal, file transfer tools, local web apps and code editors "
"with a SEPAL session*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:7
msgid ""
"Every running SEPAL session has its own **SSH login**. With it, tools on "
"your computer can connect directly to that session: you work with your "
"local programs, while your files and computations stay on SEPAL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:11
msgid "With the SSH login you can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:13
msgid "open a terminal on the session from your computer;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:14
msgid "copy files between your computer and the session;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:15
msgid ""
"open web apps running in the session, such as JupyterLab, in your local "
"browser;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:17
msgid "edit and run code on the session from a code editor, such as VS Code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:20
msgid "Get the SSH login of a session"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:22
msgid ""
"In SEPAL, start a session (for example, by opening **Terminal**). Then "
"select the hourly cost button, :btn:`<fa-solid fa-dollar-sign> x.xx/h`, "
"in the lower-right corner of the footer and choose **Sessions**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:22
msgid ""
"Hourly cost menu with the Usage and Sessions options, Sessions "
"highlighted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:33
msgid ""
"On the session you want to use, select **Copy SSH login**. The copied "
"login includes your username and the session name, for example ``alice"
"+humble-robin@ssh.sepal.io``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:33
msgid ""
"SEPAL Sessions panel with the Copy SSH login button highlighted and its "
"tooltip visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:43
msgid ""
"The examples on this page use ``alice+humble-robin@ssh.sepal.io``. "
"Replace it with the login you copied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:46
msgid "When you connect:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:48
msgid ""
"**Password or key:** enter your **SEPAL password** when prompted, or "
"register an SSH key to connect without it (see :doc:`../setup/ssh_keys`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:50
msgid ""
"**Port:** SEPAL accepts SSH connections on port **22** (the default) and "
"port **443**. If your network blocks port 22, add ``-p 443`` to ``ssh`` "
"and ``sftp`` commands, or ``-P 443`` to ``scp`` commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:53
msgid ""
"**First connection:** your SSH client shows the fingerprint of SEPAL's "
"host key and asks you to confirm it. Before confirming, compare it with "
"the published fingerprints (see :ref:`ssh_host_fingerprints`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:59
msgid ""
"The ``+session-name`` part of the login directs the connection to that "
"session. When the session stops, the connection closes and the login "
"stops working. For a new session, copy its login again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:66
msgid "Verify the host fingerprint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:68
msgid ""
"The fingerprint proves that you are connecting to SEPAL and not to "
"another server pretending to be it. On your first connection, your SSH "
"client shows a message like this one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:78
msgid ""
"Type ``yes`` only if the fingerprint matches one of the following, for "
"the key type your client shows. They are the same on ports 22 and 443:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:85
msgid "Key type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:86
msgid "Fingerprint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:87
msgid "ED25519"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:88
msgid "``SHA256:kpQFoQFHnlXRBzZNU8zrUaG7dPpuI3z3zGhe8laHx4E``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:89
msgid "ECDSA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:90
msgid "``SHA256:bgpAw63RUUdrg08L8Br9/OnILqXbWt51URergjeTgtk``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:91
msgid "RSA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:92
msgid "``SHA256:JA24YKvHYv1MXKGu2TatVQk9sxSbpMNUfgLNojuli6k``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:94
msgid ""
"Your client then remembers the key and does not ask again. If it later "
"warns that the host key has **changed**, do not connect, and report it on"
" the `SEPAL user group <https://groups.google.com/g/sepal-users>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:99
msgid "Open a terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:101
msgid ""
"In a terminal on your computer (PowerShell on Windows, Terminal on macOS "
"or Linux), run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:108
msgid ""
"You get a shell on the session, in your home folder ``/home/sepal-user``."
" Type ``exit`` to close the connection; the session keeps running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:112
msgid "Transfer files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:114
msgid ""
"Use ``scp`` to copy files and folders between your computer and the "
"session. Run these commands on your computer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:125
msgid ""
"``sftp`` and ``rsync`` work with the same login. For a graphical client, "
"see :doc:`../setup/filezilla`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:128
msgid ""
"Files copied to your home folder are kept between sessions. Files copied "
"to ``/tmp`` are deleted when the session stops (see "
":doc:`../setup/session_storage`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:132
msgid "Open web apps in your local browser"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:134
msgid ""
"A web app running in the session, such as JupyterLab, Solara or "
"Streamlit, is only reachable from inside the session. To open it in your "
"local browser, forward its port through the SSH connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:138
msgid "For example, to use JupyterLab:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:140
msgid ""
"Connect with port forwarding. ``-L 8888:localhost:8888`` forwards port "
"8888 of your computer to port 8888 of the session:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:147
msgid "In that connection, start JupyterLab without opening a browser:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:153
msgid ""
"JupyterLab prints a link that starts with "
"``http://127.0.0.1:8888/lab?token=``. Open it in your local browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:156
msgid ""
"The app runs until you stop it with :kbd:`Control-c` or close the "
"connection. To forward another app, replace ``8888`` with its port in "
"both commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:161
msgid ""
"SEPAL also runs JupyterLab, Jupyter Notebook and RStudio directly in your"
" browser from the **Apps** section, without any setup on your computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:165
msgid "Connect a code editor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:167
msgid ""
"Code editors with SSH remote development open files and run terminals, "
"debuggers and notebooks directly on the session. This section describes "
"VS Code; other editors with SSH support, such as editors based on VS Code"
" or `JetBrains Gateway <https://www.jetbrains.com/remote-"
"development/gateway/>`__, use the same SSH login."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:174
msgid "VS Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:176
msgid ""
"Before starting, install `VS Code <https://code.visualstudio.com/>`__ and"
" the `Remote - SSH extension "
"<https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ms-vscode-remote"
".remote-ssh>`__ on your computer, as well as an `SSH client "
"<https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/remote/ssh#_getting-started>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:181
msgid ""
"Open the Command Palette (**F1**) and select **Remote-SSH: Add New SSH "
"Host...**. Paste the copied login, or enter it as a full command, for "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:189
msgid ""
"Select the SSH configuration file offered by VS Code, then run **Remote-"
"SSH: Connect to Host...** and select the host you just added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:191
msgid ""
"Select **Linux** if asked for the remote platform. Enter your **SEPAL "
"password** when prompted, unless you have registered an SSH key. VS Code "
"may ask for the password more than once during setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:197
msgid ""
"The first connection can take several minutes. VS Code installs its "
"server, and later the extensions you use remotely, in ``~/.vscode-"
"server`` in your home folder. Your home folder is network storage, which "
"is slow when writing many small files (see "
":doc:`../setup/session_storage`). Later connections reuse this "
"installation and start faster, until VS Code is updated and installs a "
"new version of its server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:205
msgid ""
"Once connected, select **File > Open Folder...** and open your project "
"under ``/home/sepal-user``. The status bar shows the SSH connection; "
"terminals opened in this window run on SEPAL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:209
msgid ""
"To open Jupyter notebooks (``.ipynb`` files) in this window, install the "
"`Jupyter extension <https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName"
"=ms-toolsai.jupyter>`__ when VS Code suggests it; notebooks then run on "
"the session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:213
msgid ""
"For a new session, copy its login again and update the saved host using "
"**Remote-SSH: Open SSH Configuration File...**, or add a new host. When "
"finished, select **File > Close Remote Connection**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:217
msgid ""
"For connection problems, check **View > Output > Remote - SSH** and the "
"`VS Code SSH troubleshooting guide "
"<https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/remote/troubleshooting>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:221
msgid "Stop the session"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developers/ssh_session.rst:223
msgid ""
"Closing an SSH connection does not stop the session, which keeps "
"consuming your instance budget until it stops or expires. When you no "
"longer need it, stop it from **Sessions** in the hourly cost menu, or "
"from the **Terminal** (see :ref:`the Terminal section <terminal-"
"instances>`)."
msgstr ""

